title: Teardown, verified against Azure rather than against an exit code
subtitle: week-12-detections-as-code — cleanup.sh, 2026-11-07
width: 1020
---
$ bash week-12-detections-as-code/scripts/cleanup.sh
removing the role assignment created for the positive control...
  removed

terraform destroy...
azurerm_resource_group.detections: Destruction complete after 26s

Destroy complete! Resources: 7 destroyed.

verifying against Azure rather than against the destroy's exit code
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  resource group gone                        PASS
  Log Analytics workspace gone               PASS
  note: workspace is soft-deleted for 14 days, name still reserved
  subscription diagnostic setting gone       PASS

  teardown verified.

# Removing Sentinel does NOT remove the workspace -- Microsoft say so
# plainly. The workspace is the billable object and it survives, so the
# check asks Azure whether it is gone instead of trusting the destroy.
#
# The soft-delete note is correct behaviour, not a failure: a deleted
# Log Analytics workspace is recoverable by name for 14 days. It stops
# ingesting and stops billing, but the NAME stays reserved.
